IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part I, section 5(4) to (8): the Minister's waiver of the requirement for an application for
-- a pension, the written notice the person is owed, the statement the person must file correcting inaccuracies, the
-- person's right to decline, and the Minister's power to cancel the waiver. Every date the Act fixes for these steps
-- is "the day on which the person attains 65 years of age"; the rules below take the person's date of birth and work
-- that day out with the core's `the day on which a person born on _ attains the age of _` (fork F5 of the keel).
--
-- The Hohfeldian pairs (NOTES.md, "Jural relations"): the Minister's power to waive (5(4)) is the person's liability;
-- the Minister's duty to notify (5(5)) is the person's claim; the person's duty to correct (5(6)) is the Minister's
-- claim, with the penalty of s 44.1(1)(a.1) behind it; the person's power to decline (5(7)) is the Minister's
-- liability; the Minister's power to require an application (5(8)) is the person's liability.

§ `Limitations`

-- src:133 | (b) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
-- src:134 | Waiver of application
-- src:135 | (4) The Minister may, on the day on which a person attains 65 years of age, waive the requirement referred to in subsection (1) for an application if the Minister is satisfied, based on information that is available to him or her under this Act, that the person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2) for the payment of a pension.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(4) (src:133-135)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Minister waives the requirement for an application` IS A DATE
      `the Minister is satisfied, based on information that is available to the Minister under this Act, that the person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2) for the payment of a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` birth `the day on which the Minister waives the requirement for an application` `the Minister is satisfied, based on information that is available to the Minister under this Act, that the person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2) for the payment of a pension` MEANS
        `the day on which the Minister waives the requirement for an application` EQUALS (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65)
    AND `the Minister is satisfied, based on information that is available to the Minister under this Act, that the person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2) for the payment of a pension`

-- src:136 | Notice of intent
-- src:137 | (5) If the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of a person, the Minister shall notify the person in writing of that intention and provide them with the information on which the Minister intends to rely to approve the payment of a pension.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(5) (src:136-137)
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(5): the person is owed written notice of the intention to waive, with the information on which the Minister intends to rely` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person` MEANS
    `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person`

-- "before the day on which they attain 65 years of age": the last day is the day before the sixty-fifth birthday.
-- src:138 | Inaccuracies
-- src:139 | (6) The person shall, before the day on which they attain 65 years of age, file with the Minister a statement in which the person corrects any inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister under subsection (5).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(6) (src:138-139)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 5(6): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` birth MEANS
    (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65) MINUS 1

-- The person's duty exists where the information the Minister provided contains an inaccuracy; it is complied with by filing
-- the statement before the sixty-fifth birthday.
-- The duty to file arises only where the information contains an inaccuracy (fork OA1-F21 of NOTES.md).
-- src:138 | Inaccuracies
-- src:139 | (6) The person shall, before the day on which they attain 65 years of age, file with the Minister a statement in which the person corrects any inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister under subsection (5).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(6) (src:138-139)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 5(5) contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person files with the Minister a statement correcting the inaccuracies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(6): the person has complied` birth `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 5(5) contains an inaccuracy` `the person files with the Minister a statement correcting the inaccuracies` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        (NOT `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 5(5) contains an inaccuracy`)
    OR  (    `the person files with the Minister a statement correcting the inaccuracies`
         AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST (`s 5(6): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` birth))

-- src:140 | Declining waiver
-- src:141 | (7) The person may, before the day on which they attain 65 years of age, decline a waiver of the requirement for an application by notifying the Minister in writing of their decision to do so.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(7) (src:140-141)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      `the person notifies the Minister in writing of their decision to decline the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person notifies the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(7): the person has declined the waiver` birth `the person notifies the Minister in writing of their decision to decline the waiver` `the day on which the person notifies the Minister` MEANS
        `the person notifies the Minister in writing of their decision to decline the waiver`
    AND `the day on which the person notifies the Minister` LESS THAN (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65)

-- src:142 | Cancellation of waiver
-- src:143 | (8) Even if the requirement for an application is intended to be waived in respect of a person under subsection (4), the Minister may, before the day on which the person attains 65 years of age, require that the person make an application for payment of a pension and, in that case, the Minister shall notify the person in writing of that requirement.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(8) (src:142-143)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires that the person make an application for payment of a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Minister requires it` IS A DATE
      `the Minister notifies the person in writing of that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` birth `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person` `the Minister requires that the person make an application for payment of a pension` `the day on which the Minister requires it` `the Minister notifies the person in writing of that requirement` MEANS
        `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person`
    AND `the Minister requires that the person make an application for payment of a pension`
    AND (`the day on which the Minister requires it` LESS THAN (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65))
    AND `the Minister notifies the person in writing of that requirement`

-- The waiver as a whole: made by the Minister under 5(4), not declined under 5(7), not cancelled under 5(8).
-- src:133 | (b) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
-- src:134 | Waiver of application
-- src:135 | (4) The Minister may, on the day on which a person attains 65 years of age, waive the requirement referred to in subsection (1) for an application if the Minister is satisfied, based on information that is available to him or her under this Act, that the person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2) for the payment of a pension.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 5(4), 5(7), 5(8) (src:133-135) (src:140-143)
GIVEN `the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has declined the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required to make an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` `the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` `the person has declined the waiver` `the person is required to make an application` MEANS
        `the Minister may waive the requirement for an application`
    AND (NOT `the person has declined the waiver`)
    AND (NOT `the person is required to make an application`)
